# ADT rules the published vector set does not yet break with a case, each with the
# reason it has none. The list may only SHRINK: scripts/rule-vectors.sh fails on an
# uncovered rule that is not here, and on a listed rule that has since gained a case.
#
# A reason is not an excuse. Most of these are cases worth adding; they are listed
# because this change added the two the 0.19.1 release shipped without, not because
# the rest are unreachable.

V-TYPE a record with a type class outside the fixed set — buildable by hand, not yet built
V-ROOT a non-initial claim carrying no contributor edge, and one carrying two
V-MONO a claim whose created_at predates a reference; needs a two-claim case, unlike the single records here
V-SER a record whose keys are not CBOR Deterministic order — the set's own encoder cannot emit one
V-ALIAS a record mixing a name's alias and long form, which the set never exercises either way
V-DIFF a diff claim whose overlay contradicts the rule; the set carries no diff chain
V-DIFFEDGE the edge half of the same, and it needs the diff case first
V-ARCHIVE an archive-level rule: it judges a head and its branch table, not one record
V-TABLEREF a branch table reaching its predecessor through the wrong edge type; needs a table pair
V-REL a relation edge whose endpoints break the rule; the toy graph has no relation edge
V-IDSEQ defines id_seq(i,s) itself, and every bookmark case exercises the computation by being offered at the slot it names; a record whose own (i,s) key another slot breaks V-BMSLOT, which has its own case, so nothing is left here to break
